nt, Kirkpatrick converted to Islam and, according to Indian sources, even became a double agent working for the Hyderabadis against the East India Company.\" \"It is a remarkable story, involving secret assignations, court intrigue, harem politics, religious disputes, and espionage. But such things were not unknown: From the sixteenth century, when the Inquisition banned the Portuguese in Goa from wearing the dhoti, to the eve of the Indian Mutiny, the \"white Mughals\" who wore local dress and adopted Indian ways were a source of difficulty and embarrassment to successive colonial administrations.","pageCount":352,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social life and customs","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Race relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Outlook of Empire","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"British","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Romance","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social mores","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-white-mughals-love-and-betrayal-in-eighteenth-century-india-william-dalrymple"},{"source"